  "about": "Trading terminals, bots and wallet apps a trade can be placed through, with what identifies each on chain. This is the app, not the exchange the trade settled on. Sources: Dune Spellbook models, DefiLlama fee adapters, solana-dex-parser, the tradeSource ids of Codex, and transactions read on chain; each entry names its own in `source`. Detection order: a credit to a fee wallet (or a token account it owns), then a relayer that pays the network fee, then a router only one app invokes; on EVM a fee recipient, the router, an ERC-8021 builder code, a selector. sharedPrograms never attribute alone. Entries are observations with a date and a confidence; fee wallets and routers rotate.",
